Changes in this extraction (2026-09-15):
- Split CopyShader, ResolveShader, DepthShader and MotionShader into HLSL files.
- Renamed entry points to MainCS and documented the buffer/guide contract.
- Area weighting and nearest-depth/raw-MV sampling retain upstream semantics.
- Resolve preserves a finite original exactly for zero residual, including
  negative scene-linear values, instead of clamping that identity case.
- Resolve rejects non-finite low-resolution RGB edits per output pixel.
- For malformed non-finite native input, non-finite components become zero;
  finite components and finite alpha are preserved on that fallback path.
- Added a fixed-scale C++ contract, CPU mathematical checks and a Windows-only
  shader compiler. These are not a DLSS/NR model or a game integration.

No NVIDIA/Daniel runtime, neural model, HIP kernel, OptiScaler replacement or
frame-generation code is included. The enclosing adapter supplies a separately
documented exact-C7 helper hook and add-on installer.

